TrackFlow - Uber-like Driver Tracking Application
================================================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
TrackFlow is a real-time driver and passenger tracking application similar to Uber, built with:
- Frontend: React + Vite
- Backend: Express.js + MongoDB + Mongoose + Socket.IO
- Real-time location tracking using GPS
- Role-based authentication (drivers and passengers)
- Live map integration with Leaflet/OpenStreetMap
- Socket.IO for real-time location updates
- Swagger API documentation

FEATURES
--------
1. User Authentication
   - Driver and passenger registration/login
   - JWT-based authentication
   - Role-based access control

2. Real-time Tracking
   - Live GPS location updates from driver devices
   - Socket.IO for real-time location broadcasting
   - Geospatial queries with MongoDB 2dsphere index

3. Ride Workflow
   - Passenger requests ride
   - Nearby drivers notified
   - Driver accepts ride
   - Real-time tracking during ride
   - Ride completion and payment processing (to be implemented)

4. Map Integration
   - Leaflet.js with OpenStreetMap tiles
   - Real-time marker updates
   - Route visualization

5. API Documentation
   - Swagger/OpenAPI documentation
   - Interactive API explorer

TECHNICAL STACK
---------------
Frontend:
- React 19
- Vite 8
- React Router (for navigation)
- Leaflet.js (for maps)
- Axios (for HTTP requests)

Backend:
- Node.js
- Express.js
- MongoDB with Mongoose ODM
- Socket.IO (for real-time communication)
- JWT (for authentication)
- Bcryptjs (for password hashing)
- Dotenv (for environment variables)
- Swagger-jsdoc & Swagger-ui-express (for API docs)

SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
------------------
1. Prerequisites:
   - Node.js (v18+)
   - MongoDB (v6+)
   - Git

2. Backend Setup:
   cd backend
   npm install
   cp .env.example .env  # Edit with your MongoDB URI and JWT secret
   npm run dev

3. Frontend Setup:
   cd frontend
   npm install
   cp .env.example .env  # Edit VITE_API_URL if needed
   npm run dev

4. MongoDB Setup:
   - Ensure MongoDB is running on default port 27017
   - Database name: trackflow (will be created automatically)
   - Or update MONGODB_URI in .env file

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
---------------------
Backend (.env):
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/trackflow
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_change_in_production
PORT=5000

Frontend (.env):
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api

API ENDPOINTS
-------------
Auth:
POST /api/auth/register - Register new user (driver/passenger)
POST /api/auth/login    - Login user
GET  /api/auth/me       - Get current user profile (protected)

Users:
GET  /api/users/drivers - Get available drivers (for passengers)
PUT  /api/users/location - Update user location (requires auth)

Rides:
POST /api/rides         - Create ride request (passenger)
PUT  /api/rides/:id/accept - Accept ride (driver)
PUT  /api/rides/:id/complete - Complete ride (driver/passenger)

SOCKET.IO EVENTS
----------------
Client -> Server:
- update-location: { latitude, longitude }
- join-ride: { rideId }
- leave-ride: { rideId }

Server -> Client:
- location-updated: { userId, latitude, longitude }
- ride-status: { rideId, status, driverLocation }
- driver-location: { driverId, latitude, longitude }

ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL
-------------------------
Middleware protects routes based on user role stored in JWT token.
- Drivers can: update location, accept rides, complete rides
- Passengers can: request rides, track driver location, complete rides
- Both can: view their own profile

DEVELOPMENT COMMANDS (Windows)
------------------------------
# In backend directory:
npm run dev    # Starts server with nodemon

# In frontend directory:
npm run dev    # Starts Vite dev server

# To build for production:
# Backend: npm start (runs node server.js)
# Frontend: npm run build (creates dist folder)

NOTES
-----
- This is a MVP implementation focusing on core tracking functionality
- Payment processing, ratings, and advanced features are left for future implementation
- Production deployment would require HTTPS, proper error handling, logging, etc.
- Real GPS tracking requires mobile device permissions and background location tracking
- For mobile implementation, consider React Native or Cordova/PhoneGap

